To run:
  xta [commands]: Starts xta tool in console mode.
  xta -g:         Starts xta tool in gui mode.
Avaliable console commands:
  [-]load <xe file>: Loads the given xmos executable file
  [-]path <from ref> <to ref>: Sets a path start and end points
  [-]function <name>: Sets a path to trace a given function
  [-]proc <node id> <core id>: All following analysis on given node and core (default: 0,0)
  [-]freq <core frequency>: Sets the core freqency (default: 400)
  [-]threads <num threads>: Sets number of threads currently executing (default: 8)
  [-]list <type>: Lists all of the given <type> in the currently loaded executable
      functions: Lists the functions
      sources: Lists the files
  [-]loop <loop id> <path id> <iterations>: Sets the number of iterations for the given loop path
  [-]status: Display current status
  [-]summary <path id | level>: Display timing summary for paths/functions
      level SIMPLE: Show simple paths summary
      level COMPLETE: Show complete path(s) timing
      level COMPLETE_LOOPS: Show complete path(s) + loop timing
      level COMPLETE_BLOCKS: Show complete path(s) + loop + basic block timing
      level COMPLETE_INSTRUCTIONS: Show complete path(s) + loop + basic block + instruction timing
      level UNRESOLVED: Show unresolved path(s) timing
      level UNRESOLVED_LOOPS: Show unresolved path(s) + loop timing
      level UNRESOLVED_BLOCKS: Show unresolved path(s) + loop + basic block timing
      level UNRESOLVED_INSTRUCTIONS: Show unresolved path(s) + loop + basic block + instruction timing
      level FUNCTIONS: Show path(s) + functions summary
      level SOURCES: Show path(s) + sources summary
  [-]asm <path id>: Display annotated assembly for given path id
  [-]src <path id> <source file>: Display annotated source file for given path id
  [-]mix <path id> <source file>: Display annotated source file + assembly instructions for the given path id
  [-]trace <path id | level>: Display instruction trace for the given path id
      level COMPLETE: Trace all complete paths
      level UNRESOLVED: Trace all unresolves paths
  [-]graph: Dump graphviz dot file for previous path/function
  [-]source <file name>: Sources the given command file
  [-]history: Displays the command history
  [-]pwd: Displays the current working directory
  [-]help: Displays this help message
  [-]exit: Quits the shell
